{"sha":"2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a","node_id":"C_kwDOA-MW79oAKDJmNDc1ZTk2ODFkMmQwZTIzNmUwZmZlM2ZmZDIzMjg3MmQyZTQxNGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"William Dauchy","email":"william.dauchy@datadoghq.com","date":"2026-11-13T16:50:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-13T16:50:31Z"},"message":"http2: test that DATA on a reset stream returns the connection window (#48959)\n\nCommit Message: http2: test that DATA on a reset stream returns the\nconnection window\n\nAdditional Description:\nAdds an Envoy codec regression test for the oghttp2 connection\nflow-control window leak behind #40085 and #36188. Before\ngoogle/quiche@6c726cca (imported in #40200, backported to v1.34.3),\noghttp2 counted DATA received on a stream that the client had already\nreset against the connection window and never consumed it. Over time the\nwindow drained, and every new stream on the connection stalled after its\nresponse headers.\n\nThe test resets client streams while the server's response body is in\nflight until twice the connection window has been sent. It then checks\nthat the connection window is not exhausted and that a new stream still\nreceives its body and trailers. It passes for nghttp2 and oghttp2 on\nmain. With the QUICHE fix reverted (`--override_module`), the oghttp2\nvariant fails: the server's connection send window is 0, and the new\nstream gets its headers but no data or trailers, matching #36188.\n\nRisk Level: Low (test only)\nTesting: `bazel test //test/common/http/http2:codec_impl_test\n--test_filter='*DataAfterClientResetReturnsConnectionWindow*'`, on main\nand with the QUICHE fix reverted.\nDocs Changes: N/A\nRelease Notes: N/A\nPlatform Specific Features: N/A\n\nAI disclosure: investigated and drafted with an AI coding assistant; I\nreviewed and understand the change.\n\nSigned-off-by: William Dauchy <william.dauchy@datadoghq.com>","tree":{"sha":"63a8c12ed7d21bf90340dd81521aa22b5f1aa2fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/git/trees/63a8c12ed7d21bf90340dd81521aa22b5f1aa2fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/git/commits/2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq9z/XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn8MQAHWRcBpSaIMTWu5K/9bGkAfg\naqJOtuMhVD8hVzNZIuKsZMHx+A4Hq21aK7avwIxuKr2X/n/AsmN9ZjxOzJ9OSxkN\nZBDzZCvKQj+PmEqezcR02Mzl/fLnUHGCEX441wPJZ/eJDPU9STyuM2Mf/led9ILc\ncZDnVbtOp/prqvF0AxyuWs7Sx/q60HYl/oWhkkan22eezBbcmRZ4mfJib6qTjLh6\n9tYi78i9kZl/Q45BwUC5PXORqegNey86js1tuwlDryUIQU/E47VHPh9LyZ8s+8l7\nnIwhZf+wvrmqF9vbhO3QHN+4Hsr96W7T6mntIs7GCiulzp8nsw9AfI33c/QNQfO3\nM05UBvRGwnU49jQlQ4rXyJi6dSdwGq+7bhYv/f4oGxhh1CDyJKMU0O0SYJ7QA+Vc\nm2N0aECdqtpukhC+oeMeD0Ku2iQ9kPI84VflKQa34iuG58wRfQ1t2/4naZo11dx1\nq4MTsp3OOMJSi/VWDyWy9CSIqKgEgK5gF2v4TYngGR8IpHgV9UlG7iUvmWH5bqcL\n1e3BPFbgmkk8K9PuXGwcGogPAQqd3QwMAdWOcTIWATQ+Pih2sQHhPUnQvSoIh2Fq\n3eHJeA9HyabYrZTKO0GJ6Q4u0O+24PETkkqoHzru1F4DMywp6VQCcMUnH14Sjr39\nuZedK4cyia+3S0y37Llz\n=b4Ae\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 63a8c12ed7d21bf90340dd81521aa22b5f1aa2fc\nparent bef6a20bb9b091e0f4af002fa83500ce96744804\nauthor William Dauchy <william.dauchy@datadoghq.com> 1794588631 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1794588631 -0500\n\nhttp2: test that DATA on a reset stream returns the connection window (#48959)\n\nCommit Message: http2: test that DATA on a reset stream returns the\nconnection window\n\nAdditional Description:\nAdds an Envoy codec regression test for the oghttp2 connection\nflow-control window leak behind #40085 and #36188. Before\ngoogle/quiche@6c726cca (imported in #40200, backported to v1.34.3),\noghttp2 counted DATA received on a stream that the client had already\nreset against the connection window and never consumed it. Over time the\nwindow drained, and every new stream on the connection stalled after its\nresponse headers.\n\nThe test resets client streams while the server's response body is in\nflight until twice the connection window has been sent. It then checks\nthat the connection window is not exhausted and that a new stream still\nreceives its body and trailers. It passes for nghttp2 and oghttp2 on\nmain. With the QUICHE fix reverted (`--override_module`), the oghttp2\nvariant fails: the server's connection send window is 0, and the new\nstream gets its headers but no data or trailers, matching #36188.\n\nRisk Level: Low (test only)\nTesting: `bazel test //test/common/http/http2:codec_impl_test\n--test_filter='*DataAfterClientResetReturnsConnectionWindow*'`, on main\nand with the QUICHE fix reverted.\nDocs Changes: N/A\nRelease Notes: N/A\nPlatform Specific Features: N/A\n\nAI disclosure: investigated and drafted with an AI coding assistant; I\nreviewed and understand the change.\n\nSigned-off-by: William Dauchy <william.dauchy@datadoghq.com>","verified_at":"2026-11-13T16:50:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/commits/2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a","html_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/commit/2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/commits/2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a/comments","author":{"login":"wdauchy","id":104408,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDQwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104408?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy","html_url":"https://github.com/wdauchy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdauchy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bef6a20bb9b091e0f4af002fa83500ce96744804","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/commits/bef6a20bb9b091e0f4af002fa83500ce96744804","html_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/commit/bef6a20bb9b091e0f4af002fa83500ce96744804"}],"stats":{"total":51,"additions":51,"deletions":0},"files":[{"sha":"93e313be255bc1a04a0f0ff5087c1492dcaeedf2","filename":"test/common/http/http2/codec_impl_test.cc","status":"modified","additions":51,"deletions":0,"changes":51,"blob_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a/test%2Fcommon%2Fhttp%2Fhttp2%2Fcodec_impl_test.cc","raw_url":"https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/raw/2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a/test%2Fcommon%2Fhttp%2Fhttp2%2Fcodec_impl_test.cc","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/envoyproxy/envoy/contents/test%2Fcommon%2Fhttp%2Fhttp2%2Fcodec_impl_test.cc?ref=2f475e9681d2d0e236e0ffe3ffd232872d2e414a","patch":"@@ -2399,6 +2399,57 @@ TEST_P(Http2CodecImplFlowControlTest, PendingRecvBufferBoundedWhenDeferProcessin\n   }\n }\n \n+// Verify that DATA the client receives on a stream it already reset is returned to the\n+// connection flow-control window. If it is not, the window drains and every later stream on the\n+// connection stalls after its response headers.\n+// See https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/issues/36188 and\n+// https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/issues/40085.\n+TEST_P(Http2CodecImplFlowControlTest, DataAfterClientResetReturnsConnectionWindow) {\n+  initialize();\n+\n+  TestRequestHeaderMapImpl request_headers;\n+  HttpTestUtility::addDefaultHeaders(request_headers);\n+  TestResponseHeaderMapImpl response_headers{{\":status\", \"200\"}};\n+  EXPECT_CALL(request_decoder_, decodeHeaders_(_, true)).Times(AnyNumber());\n+  EXPECT_CALL(response_decoder_, decodeHeaders_(_, false)).Times(AnyNumber());\n+  EXPECT_CALL(server_stream_callbacks_, onResetStream(_, _)).Times(AnyNumber());\n+  EXPECT_CALL(server_codec_event_callbacks_, onCodecLowLevelReset()).Times(AnyNumber());\n+\n+  // Send twice the connection window on streams that the client resets while the server's\n+  // response body is in flight.\n+  const uint32_t initial_connection_window = getSendWindowSize(server_);\n+  ASSERT_EQ(65535, initial_connection_window);\n+  const uint32_t body_size = 16 * 1024;\n+  for (uint32_t sent = 0; sent < 2 * initial_connection_window; sent += body_size) {\n+    EXPECT_OK(request_encoder_->encodeHeaders(request_headers, true));\n+    driveToCompletion();\n+    response_encoder_->encodeHeaders(response_headers, false);\n+    driveToCompletion();\n+\n+    // The client's RST_STREAM is still in flight when the server sends the body.\n+    request_encoder_->getStream().resetStream(StreamResetReason::LocalReset);\n+    Buffer::OwnedImpl body(std::string(body_size, 'a'));\n+    response_encoder_->encodeData(body, false);\n+    driveToCompletion();\n+\n+    request_encoder_ = &client_->newStream(response_decoder_);\n+  }\n+  EXPECT_GT(getSendWindowSize(server_), 0);\n+\n+  // A new stream on the same connection still gets its body and trailers.\n+  EXPECT_OK(request_encoder_->encodeHeaders(request_headers, true));\n+  driveToCompletion();\n+  response_encoder_->encodeHeaders(response_headers, false);\n+  Buffer::OwnedImpl body(\"hello\");\n+  response_encoder_->encodeData(body, false);\n+  response_encoder_->encodeTrailers(TestResponseTrailerMapImpl{{\"grpc-status\", \"0\"}});\n+  EXPECT_CALL(response_decoder_, decodeData(_, false));\n+  EXPECT_CALL(response_decoder_, decodeTrailers_(_));\n+  driveToCompletion();\n+  EXPECT_OK(client_wrapper_->status_);\n+  EXPECT_OK(server_wrapper_->status_);\n+}\n+\n // Verify that we create and disable the stream flush timer when trailers follow a stream that\n // does not have enough window.\n TEST_P(Http2CodecImplFlowControlTest, TrailingHeadersLargeServerBody) {"}]}